<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ishida Mitsunari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1560–1600</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ishida Mitsunari was a Japanese warlord and administrator, one of the five commissioners who ran the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>. After Hideyoshi's death he organised the western coalition against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a>, which was defeated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Battle of Sekigahara</a> in 1600. He was captured and executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>, and his lands at Sawayama were given to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ii-naomasa">Ii Naomasa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ishida-mitsunari.jpg" alt="Ishida Mitsunari" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ishida_Mitsunari.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
